---
import { songUrl, songUrlBySlug, hasPage } from '../lib/songs.js';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, href } from '../lib/site.js';
import releases from '../data/releases.json';
import songs from '../data/songs.json';

// Keeps "Our story" current: names the newest release unless the story already does.
const singlesLine = 'Since then, West Coast Revival has shared new songs with churches one at a time, starting in 2019 with "Behold Our God (Almost Acoustic)" and continuing through "Flesh and Blood," "The Armor" and "We Three Kings." "The Sparrow" followed in 2021, alongside <em>Oh the Deep</em>, a refreshed edition of the original <em>FUSE</em> songs. 2022 brought "Before My Knees Could Reach the Ground," and 2025 saw "Solid Rock," "In You Is Mercy" and "Have You Been to Jesus."';
const latestTitle = releases.latest?.title || songs.find((s) => !s.unreleased)?.title;
const latestDate = releases.latest?.date ? new Date(releases.latest.date + 'T12:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' }) : null;
const latestSlug = songs.find((x) => x.title.toLowerCase() === (latestTitle || '').toLowerCase())?.slug;
const showLatest = latestTitle && !singlesLine.toLowerCase().includes(latestTitle.toLowerCase());
---
<Base title="About" description="About West Coast Revival: brothers Jonathan and Ryan Baird, the songs they write for the church, and the nonprofit ministry behind them." image="/img/brothers-portrait-800.webp" current="about">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid two" style="align-items:center">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Timeless truth. Untamed affection.</h1>
        <p class="lead">{SITE.mission}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo"><img width="800" height="832" src="/img/brothers-portrait-800.webp" alt="Brothers Ryan and Jonathan Baird" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Why we serve the church through song</h2>
      <p>There is something special about the gift of music that God has given man. It has a unique ability to communicate truths about God that transcend mere words and speech. It continually amazes us how God structured the universe to work, and music, we believe, is a language He intended to be used to bring us out of the earthly and experience the divine.</p>
      <p>From the beginning, Jonathan and I have desired to write music that lifts our eyes to the divine, because that's what we believe God built into our DNA. In singing and hearing music written with words that exalt and magnify the greatness of God, and specifically the life, death, resurrection, ascension and return of Jesus Christ, God uses that to show us more of Himself.</p>
      <p>That is why West Coast Revival exists as a nonprofit ministry: to write songs that local churches can sing, and to give churches, worship teams and communities the songs, charts and teaching to worship Christ together, free of charge.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid two" style="align-items:start">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Our story</h2>
        <p>Brothers Jonathan and Ryan have been leading worship and writing songs for the church together for decades. They began West Coast Revival in 2003, and in 2005 their first collection of congregational songs, <em>FUSE</em>, was published with Sovereign Grace Music, followed by a full-length collection in 2007.</p>
        <p>They went on to write for Sovereign Grace Music projects used in churches, including "Behold Our God" in 2011. Joined by their sister Meghan Baird, they published two more collections of songs for congregations, <em>All That Thrills My Soul</em> and <em>Some Bright Golden Morning</em> (2015).</p>
        <p set:html={singlesLine} />
        {showLatest && (
          <p>Their newest song for churches is {latestSlug ? <a href={href(songUrlBySlug(latestSlug))}>"{latestTitle}"</a> : `"${latestTitle}"`}{latestDate ? `, out ${latestDate}` : ''}.</p>
        )}
        <p>The best place to find new songs and teaching from West Coast Revival is <a href={href('/worship-is-warfare')}>Worship Is Warfare</a>, live every Tuesday and Thursday at 6am MST. It's a live broadcast and podcast on worship as spiritual warfare: the fight to make Christ our greatest delight.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid" style="gap:16px">
        <div class="photo"><img width="800" height="1200" src="/img/jon-worship-800.webp" alt="Jonathan Baird in worship" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <div class="photo"><img width="800" height="533" src="/img/ryan-best-800.webp" alt="Ryan Baird singing at the keys" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
